# `@: Model m @ Model 3` with nothing reading m: a reference declaration whose candidate is one value and one more
# is refused at the extra value, whether or not anything reads the name (DECLARATION-CANDIDATE-ROLE,
# steps/defects.md). It was taken for a machine local with the model; its L1 joined the 3 to the address
# (`lmx_arena_ref_struct(node, 0U)3`), which gcc refused.
Model:
    int: value 7
end: Model
fn: check () int
    @: Model m @ Model 3
    return: 7
end: check
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
